---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Sandbox" sheep={false}>
  <header class="post-head">
    <h1>The mechanistic sandbox</h1>
    <p class="meta">runs 100% in your browser · demos 2 and 3 download a 23&nbsp;MB model on first use · demo 4 is my own 45k-parameter model</p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>I built this sandbox for the classes I TA, then decided to put it online for anyone to play with.</p>

    <h2>1. Tokenization</h2>
    <p>Before an LLM can understand language, it chops words into subword “tokens.” See how GPT-4 slices up rare words like <em>indubitably</em> in <a href="https://platform.openai.com/tokenizer">OpenAI’s tokenizer sandbox</a>.</p>

    <h2>2. Embeddings</h2>
    <p>How does a network know that <em>“The monarch rested”</em> is close to <em>“The king sat”</em> when they barely share a word? We embed both with <code>all-MiniLM-L6-v2</code> into 384 dimensions and take the cosine similarity.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card demo">
    <input type="text" id="sem-input-1" placeholder="The king sat on the throne" />
    <input type="text" id="sem-input-2" placeholder="The monarch rested on his chair" />
    <div class="sim-row">
      <div class="track"><div id="similarity-bar"></div></div>
      <span id="similarity-score">0.00</span>
    </div>
    <div id="sem-progress-container" class="progress" style="display:none"><div id="sem-progress-bar"></div></div>
    <p class="meta" id="sem-status">Click a box to load the model.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>3. Live token-similarity map</h2>
    <p>Type a sentence and hover a token to see which other tokens its final-layer representation is closest to. This is <em>not</em> attention: the WASM build drops the attention tensors, so what you get is cosine similarity between final-layer token states — a rough visual proxy, and worth knowing the difference.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card demo" style="text-align:center">
    <input type="text" id="matrix-input" placeholder="The quick brown fox" />
    <div id="matrix-progress-container" class="progress" style="display:none"><div id="matrix-progress-bar"></div></div>
    <p class="meta" id="matrix-status">Click the box to load the model.</p>
    <div id="matrix-hover-container" class="tokens"></div>
    <p class="meta" id="matrix-helper" style="display:none">Hover a token.</p>
    <div id="matrix-grid-container" style="display:flex;justify-content:center;overflow-x:auto"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>4. Induction heads, live</h2>
    <p>This is a real transformer running in your browser: two layers of four attention heads, no MLPs, about 45k parameters, computed from its weights as you type. I <a href="https://github.com/mehdievaltimes/mehdievaltimes.github.io/blob/main/scripts/induction/train.py">trained it</a> on random characters with stretches that repeat. Random characters can’t be predicted, so the only way to do better than chance is to notice the text repeating and copy what came next last time.</p>
    <p>That takes two heads working together, an <a href="https://transformer-circuits.pub/2022/in-context-learning-and-induction-heads/index.html">induction circuit</a>. A <em>previous-token head</em> in layer 0 tags every position with the character before it. An <em>induction head</em> in layer 1 then looks for an earlier position tagged with the current character, and copies what’s there. The labels below come from measuring each head on a repeated random string when the page loads; nothing is hard-coded.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="card demo ih" id="induction">
    <div class="ih-presets">
      <button type="button" class="chip" data-preset="random">random, twice</button>
      <button type="button" class="chip" data-preset="the cat sat on the mat. the cat sat on the mat.">a sentence, twice</button>
      <button type="button" class="chip" data-preset="mr qwibble and mrs zarkov met at the kalshi office. later, mr qwibble">a name comes back</button>
    </div>
    <input type="text" id="ih-input" maxlength="99" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" value="vk9 quorx blimp-fizz! vk9 quorx blimp-fizz!" aria-label="Text for the model" />
    <p class="meta" id="ih-status">Loading the model (230 KB)…</p>
    <div class="ih-text" id="ih-text" aria-label="Each character, with a bar for how likely the model thought it was"></div>
    <p class="meta" id="ih-stats" aria-live="polite"></p>
    <p class="meta" id="ih-query"></p>
    <div class="ih-split">
      <div>
        <div class="ih-heads" id="ih-heads"></div>
        <p class="meta">Click a head to show it. <em>Knock out</em> removes its output from the residual stream. The model learned four induction heads, so knocking out one barely matters; it takes all four. But it leans on one previous-token head, and knocking out just that one stops the copying. <button type="button" class="linkish" id="ih-reset">restore all</button></p>
      </div>
      <figure class="ih-big">
        <canvas id="ih-big"></canvas>
        <figcaption class="meta"><span id="ih-big-title"></span> · row = the position looking, column = where it looks</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
    <p class="meta" id="ih-train"></p>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>More</h2>
    <p><a href="/puppy-bench">Puppy bench</a>: a one-task safety eval. Each model controls a robot body and is told to use a <code>kill_puppy</code> tool. Some do.</p>
  </div>

  <script is:inline type="module" src="/js/demos.js"></script>
  <script is:inline src="/js/induction.js"></script>
</Base>

<style is:global>
  @media (min-width: 64rem) { main:has(.demo) { max-width: 46rem; } }
  .demo { margin: 1.25rem 0 2.5rem; display: grid; gap: .6rem; }
  .sim-row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 1rem; margin-top: .5rem; }
  .track { flex: 1; height: 10px; background: var(--faint); border-radius: 99px; overflow: hidden; }
  #similarity-bar { height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--accent); transition: width .3s; }
  #similarity-score { font: 500 1.1rem var(--mono); min-width: 3.5rem; text-align: right; }
  .progress { height: 4px; background: var(--faint); border-radius: 99px; overflow: hidden; }
  .progress > div { height: 100%; width: 0; background: var(--accent); transition: width .1s; }
  .demo .meta { margin: 0; }
  .tokens { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; justify-content: center; gap: .4rem; }
  .word-token { padding: .3rem .7rem; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid var(--faint); background: var(--bg); cursor: pointer; font: .95rem var(--mono); transition: background-color .15s, border-color .15s; }
  .word-token.active { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .matrix-table { border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1.5rem auto; }
  .matrix-cell { width: 34px; height: 34px; text-align: center; font: .7rem var(--mono); border: 1px solid var(--faint); cursor: crosshair; }
  .matrix-cell:hover { outline: 2px solid var(--fg); position: relative; }
  .matrix-header-col { writing-mode: vertical-rl; transform: rotate(180deg); padding: 6px; font: .75rem var(--mono); text-align: left; white-space: nowrap; }
  .matrix-header-row { padding: 6px; font: .75rem var(--mono); text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }

  .ih-presets { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: .4rem; }
  .ih:not(.ready) .ih-text, .ih:not(.ready) .ih-split { display: none; }
  .ih-text { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 2px; margin-top: .4rem; }
  .ih-ch { all: unset; box-sizing: border-box; width: 1.35rem; height: 3.1rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; padding: .25rem 0 .2rem; border-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; font: .95rem var(--mono); border: 1px solid transparent; }
  .ih-ch:first-child { width: 2rem; font-size: .7rem; color: var(--muted); }
  .ih-ch i { display: block; width: .55rem; background: var(--good); border-radius: 2px 2px 0 0; opacity: .85; }
  .ih-ch.q { border-color: var(--fg); }
  .ih-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto; gap: 1.2rem; align-items: start; margin-top: .6rem; }
  .ih-heads { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: .5rem; }
  .ih-heads + .meta { margin-top: .8rem; }
  .ih-head { text-align: center; font: .68rem var(--mono); color: var(--muted); }
  .ih-pick { all: unset; cursor: pointer; display: block; border-radius: 4px; border: 2px solid transparent; line-height: 0; }
  .ih-pick canvas { border-radius: 2px; max-width: 100%; height: auto !important; }
  .ih-head.selected .ih-pick { border-color: var(--accent); }
  .ih-head.off .ih-pick { opacity: .25; }
  .ih-name { color: var(--fg); margin-top: .2rem; }
  .ih-kind { color: var(--accent); min-height: 1.2em; }
  .ih-ko { font-size: .68rem; text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
  .ih-big { margin: 0; }
  .ih-big canvas { display: block; border-radius: 4px; border: 1px solid var(--faint); }
  .ih-big figcaption { margin-top: .3rem; max-width: 320px; }
  @media (max-width: 44rem) { .ih-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
